  {
   "id": "title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1500,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 900,
   "height": 120,
   "text": "# Minideck \u2014 power wiring\n25 wires \u00b7 generated from the wiring plan (`python3 wiring_canvas.py`)"
  },
  {
   "id": "legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -560,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 320,
   "height": 112,
   "text": "**Wire colours**\n- <span style=\"color:#e03131\">\u25a0</span> 5 V / battery +\n- <span style=\"color:#868e96\">\u25a0</span> GND\n- <span style=\"color:#f08c00\">\u25a0</span> 3.3 V"
  },
  {
   "id": "notes",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -200,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 720,
   "height": 216,
   "text": "**Notes**\n- Boost: Pololu U3V40F5, fixed 5 V (nothing to adjust), ~2.6 A out from a charged cell.\n- Load is taken from the TP4056's B+/B\u2212 pads, so its ~3 A protection is not in the power path: use a protected high-drain 18650 (button top, \u226470 mm).\n- TP4056 = charging only; its OUT pads stay empty. Charging works with the switch off.\n- Power switch: middle pin from B+, one outer pin to the boost VIN (check the ON end with a meter).\n- 47 \u00b5F capacitor right across the boost's input pads.\n- Battery \u2192 charger \u2192 switch \u2192 boost: 20\u201322 AWG; splice \u2192 loads: 24 AWG."
  }
 ],
